  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shaukatali Khusiyal Pathan vs The State Of Maharashtra on 21 December, 2023 Author: M. S. Karnik Bench: M. S. Karnik 2023:Bhc-As:38873 Darshan Patil 941-ba-4112-23.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Bail Application No. 4112 Of 2023 Shaukatali Khusiyal Pathan ..Applicant Vs. The State Of Maharashtra ..Respondent ------------ Adv. Tushar Sonawane for the Applicant. Mr. Y. Y. Dabke, App for the State. ------------ Coram : M. S. Karnik, J. Date : December 21, 2023 P.C. : 1. 2. This is an application for bail in respect of the offence punishable under Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 of the Indian Penal Code (IPC) and Sections 26(2)(i), 27(3)(e), 3(1)(zz) (iv), 26(2)(e), 59 and 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 registered on 11/10/2023 vide C.R. No.535 of 2023 with Kalwa Police Station.",
    "facts": "2. This is an application for bail in respect of the offence punishable under Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 of the Indian Penal Code (IPC) and Sections 26(2)(i), 27(3)(e), 3(1)(zz) (iv), 26(2)(e), 59 and 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 registered on 11/10/2023 vide C.R. No.535 of 2023 with Kalwa Police Station. The materials recovered are scented pan masala and scented tobacco. The question whether the offence under Section 328 is attracted to the materials in question is pending consideration before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. 4. It is alleged that on 11/10/2023, one vehicle was intercepted at Kharegaon toll naka. The vehicle was driven by the one Manjitkumar Gango Rai. The applicant is the transporter, in whose truck the goods seized were to be delivered to the concerned person. The entire material has been seized. 5. Learned APP opposed the application and submitted that there are 3 criminal antecedents against the applicant. 6. The applicant was arrested on 22/11/2023.",
